    │   granular flags); eventlet and gevent have different greenlet implementations; code that directly uses greenlet primitives 
    │   may need adjustment; socketio.run() with eventlet uses eventlet's WSGI server; gevent would require gunicorn + gevent 
    │   worker or gevent.pywsgi for production; threading model differences: eventlet uses green threads via greenlet; gevent uses
    │   greenlet but with different scheduling semantics
    └── Both eventlet and gevent provide greenlet-based cooperative concurrency with monkey-patching of the standard library 
        (socket, threading, time, etc.) to make blocking I/O cooperative. The code uses eventlet.monkey_patch() at startup, which 
        is the canonical entry point for both libraries. gevent.monkey.patch_all() serves the same purpose and is a near drop-in 
        replacement for this usage pattern.

